---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import Architecture from '../../components/Architecture.astro';
import { projects, meridianStudy as study } from '../../data/portfolio';
const project = projects[0];
---
<Layout title="Meridian — Personal Finance Assistant | Mahmoud Heshmat" description="A personal finance assistant case study: transaction ingestion, reported ML evaluation, FastAPI architecture, and the boundaries of the available evidence.">
  <div class="container case-study">
    <a class="back-link" href="/#work"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All selected work</a>
    <header class="case-header"><p class="eyebrow accent">Independent project / Engineering case study</p><h1>Meridian<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p class="serif case-subtitle">From transactions to a clearer picture.</p><p class="lead">A personal finance assistant connecting test banking data, spending categorization, and monthly forecasting.</p><div class="actions"><span class="status-label">{project.status}</span><a class="text-link" href={project.repository}>Explore the repository <Arrow external /></a></div></header>
    <aside class="evidence-notice"><span class="eyebrow accent">Reading this case study</span><p>The finance MVP and evaluation results below are owner-reported. Inspection of the current repository confirms backend and data-processing code, but its README now describes a RAG roadmap and its core categorizer uses keyword rules. The XGBoost/Prophet results have not been independently reproduced. These differences are kept explicit.</p></aside>
    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Case study contents"><a href="#problem">01 / Context</a><a href="#architecture">02 / Architecture</a><a href="#decisions">03 / Decisions</a><a href="#evaluation">04 / Evaluation</a><a href="#limitations">05 / Limitations</a></nav>
    <section id="problem" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow accent">01 / Context</p><h2>Make spending<br /><span class="serif">understandable.</span></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>{study.problem}</p><h3>Implemented scope & status</h3><p>{project.scope} Docker Compose is provided for local development. The existence of infrastructure files does not verify that a deployment is currently online.</p><h3>My contribution</h3><p>{study.contribution}</p></div></section>
    <section id="architecture" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow accent">02 / Architecture</p><h2>A pipeline, an API,<br /><span class="serif">two ML tasks.</span></h2><p class="muted">The conceptual finance workflow is based on the supplied MVP description.</p></div><div><Architecture /><div class="prose"><h3>What is inspectable in the repository</h3><p><code>core.py</code> normalizes CSV and Plaid-shaped transaction payloads, applies keyword categorization, and aggregates spending. Docker Compose defines an API service, PostgreSQL with pgvector, and Redis. ECS Terraform modules describe cloud infrastructure.</p><p>Document ingestion and Titan embedding code also exist under <code>ai/</code>. They belong to the repository’s retrieval work and are not evidence that the finance MVP uses the Multi-Agent Platform.</p></div></div></section>
    <section id="decisions" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow accent">03 / Engineering decisions</p><h2>Choices, context,<br /><span class="serif">and boundaries.</span></h2></div><div class="decision-list">{study.decisions.map((decision, index) => <article><span class="eyebrow accent">0{index + 1}</span><div><h3>{decision.title}</h3><p>{decision.text}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="evaluation" class="evaluation-section"><p class="eyebrow accent">04 / Evaluation</p><h2>Results need <span class="serif">their context.</span></h2><p class="evaluation-intro">Reported experiments on test and synthetic data. These are not production performance claims.</p><div class="evaluation-grid">{study.evaluations.map(result => <article><span class="metric serif">{result.value}</span><h3>{result.label}</h3><p>{result.context}</p></article>)}</div><p class="small muted">Evaluation artifacts were not found in the inspected revision. No independent model run was performed for this portfolio.</p></section>
    <section id="limitations" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow accent">05 / Limitations & next steps</p><h2>A clear boundary<br /><span class="serif">for every claim.</span></h2></div><div class="prose"><ul class="limitation-list">{study.limitations.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p>Next steps are to reconcile the finance and RAG documentation, publish reproducible evaluation artifacts, and provide a demo URL if an accessible deployment is available. These are documentation and validation goals, not completed deliverables.</p><a class="text-link" href={project.repository}>Inspect the source on GitHub <Arrow external /></a></div></section>
    <div class="case-end"><a class="text-link" href="/#work">← Back to selected work</a><a class="text-link" href="/#contact">Let’s connect <Arrow /></a></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
